    "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `--mamba-ssm-dtype bfloat16`, the KDA SSM pool is bf16. `_kda_track_ssm_kernel` (#41105) loads the pool dtype in its mode-1 branch and the fp32 chunk-boundary snapshot in its mode-2 branch, then stores the result. Triton rejects a variable whose type differs between the branches of a runtime `if`, so the kernel fails to compile on a bf16 pool. On GLM-5.3-Flash with breakable prefill CUDA graphs, which capture the KDA extend, this fails server startup during prefill graph capture.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Cast the fp32 snapshot to the pool dtype inside the mode-2 branch, so both branches produce the pool dtype. An fp32 pool is unaffected: the cast is then a no-op.\n- Add `test_kda_prefill_graph_track.py`. It runs `kda_track_ssm_state` on fp32 and bf16 pools with mode 0, 1 and 2 rows, and compares the pool exactly with a torch reference.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nOn an RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (SM120) with Triton 3.8.0, the new test passes (2 tests). Without the kernel change, the bf16 case fails to compile.\n\nA GLM-5.3-Flash FP8 TP4 server with `--mamba-ssm-dtype bfloat16` and `--cuda-graph-backend-prefill breakable` failed at startup without this change. With it, the server started and served.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: the fp32 path is unchanged, and the bf16 path did not compile before.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\nDeveloped with AI assistance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38118289730](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38118289730)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38118289559](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38118289559)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38118289675](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38118289675)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
